@startuml v1-daemon
' Revision (2026-10-13): accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
title Companion to M-DP1: service from slice 0; later capabilities and gated SH2+ backend
participant "Caller process\ncaller UID / principal + key" as C
participant "Read-only account\nswarma-observer" as R
participant "swarma-dispatcher daemon\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher\nadmission, records, claims, effects, cleanup" as D
participant "swarma-session-host\nSH2+ own service UID\nmetadata, logs, receipts, fences, input admission" as SH
participant "swarma-user-launcher\nroot until agent UID drop; receipt writer" as L
participant "swarma-session-runner\nSH2+ agent UID\nPTY/app-server and renewal" as SR
participant "Credential broker\nunprivileged; binding / grant / lease owner" as B
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; account ledger / stop evidence" as H
D -> D : closed admission; ownership/schema/replay/authentication -> controls\nclassify/account/confine unresolved effects -> forward readiness
C -> D : dispatch/1 connect; peer UID; verify server UID; hello; signed request
alt daemon absent or authentication / permission / version / malformed response failure
  break transport refusal
    C -> C : refuse; no command fallback
  end
else ambiguous reply
  C -> D : repeat same request_id and signature
end
opt forward admission closed but valid control surface
  C -> D : authorised status/list/reconcile or current-execution stop
  D --> C : observations/stop intent; retained unknown claims; no launch grant needed
end
opt operator state read after control prerequisites
  R -> D : status/list and dispatcher state reads; no confirmation
  D --> R : read-only state; no mutation authority
end
D -> D : forward request requires readiness; prepare principal/signature/chains, quota\nrecorded class, qualified host matrix, machine-selected exec identity/body pin\ntrusted provider-only network pin; caller text checked, never authority
D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context prepare
B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + revocation sequence
alt quota / authority failure or revoked / unavailable
  break permanent refusal
    D --> C : refuse before new effects; never queue
  end
else temporary capacity closure
  alt initial slice
    break capacity refusal
      D --> C : capacity:*; no queue
    end
  else later queue capability enabled
    D -> D : persist bounded fair queue
    D --> C : queued handle
    ... gate opens ...
    D -> D : recheck principal, signature/window, quota and all gates
    D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context dequeue
    B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + sequence
    alt authority / quota / window refuses or revoked / unavailable
      break no forward effect
        D --> C : refuse
      end
    else capacity remains closed
      break remain queued
        D -> D : retain durable queue; no launch
      end
    end
  end
end
== admitted request only ==
D -> D : provision with journaled distinct effects
note over D
  Standing start: max_runtime absent; supplied duration refuses before launch.
  Standing execution: no runtime quota or deadline in either backend.
  Ordinary execution: default 4 h, maximum 12 h (§§3.5, 8.1).
  Standing max_runtime refusal-code mapping is unpublished (§16, question 8).
end note
alt SH2+ permit / ownership / crash-order gates published and qualified (§§12, 14)
  C -> D : owner-signed start; session lifecycle authorisation if successors allowed
  D -> D : retain authorisation + immutable plan in input/session record
  SH -> SH : persist session intent and closed delivery fence
  D -> D : recheck owner start authority/lifetime/runtime policy
  D -> B : fresh revocation.check exact chains, context start
  B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable
  alt owner admission invalid or revoked / unavailable
    break no admitted permit or physical start
      D --> C : refuse
    end
  end
  D -> D : admit owner start; durable session-scoped host admission permit
  note over C,SH
    Permit is for one logical_session_id; one-start request admits no successor.
    Owner chain remains binding dependency; host acquires no spawn/lease chain.
    Lifecycle member / permit reference / auth encoding unpublished (§16).
  end note
  SH -> D : host_start (logical_session_id, execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id)
  D -> D : authenticate configured host; verify session permit + per-use fence\nlocal lock + in-flight marker; release for every receiver call
  alt successor physical start
    D -> D : look up durable (logical_session_id, op_id) replay first
    opt exact recorded replay
      break return same successor/evidence; no physical start
        D --> SH : current recorded successor; never create another
      end
    end
    D -> D : require owner lifecycle consent; unchanged stored plan, no host plan bytes
    D -> D : previous claim confirmed absent or agent_busy; no ordinary lifetime/budget reset
    D -> D : retain replay identity with distinct successor record/effects
  end
  D -> D : recheck active original owner principal, signature, chain/window; current fences
  D -> B : fresh revocation.check exact chains, context start
  B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + sequence
  alt revoked / unavailable or original authority invalid
    break no physical start
      D --> SH : refuse; permit never replaces owner consent/current authority
    end
  end
  alt wrong principal / mismatched permit values / stale epoch / withdrawn permit
    break no launcher call
      D --> SH : refuse; live pid is not controller authority
    end
  else fence changed or cancelled before call issue
    D -> D : durable withdrawal/cancel intent under local lock; prevent call
  else physical call admitted
    D -> D : own execution_id/controller_epoch/op_id claim + fence\nlocal lock: journal distinct E-launch and in-flight marker; unlock
    D -> L : launch.start; no state lock held; dispatcher-owned effect / root receipt path
    alt root call ambiguous
      D -> D : resolve same effect and root receipt; never launch twice
      opt stop required after resolution
        D -> H : exec.stop with original authorized stop effect
        H --> D : confirmed execution absence, or unknown/refused stays pending
      end
    else root call accepted
      D -> D : local lock: revalidate result/fences; stale result is historical evidence only
      L -> L : user-manager §7 R-FD3 lifecycle; root receipt before UID/GID drop
      L -> SR : approved runner; only 0-2 + staged immutable read-only FD3
      SR -> SH : fresh authenticated channel; current-epoch registration
      SR -> B : own qualified lease and renewal; final broker checks mandatory
      SR -> SH : readiness
      SH -> SH : validate current epoch/fence; permit delivery only after ready registration
    end
  end
  opt host failure, mid-call cancel or fence change spanning physical start
    SH -> D : request durable withdrawal (encoding unpublished); no host fence lock held
    D -> D : record cancel intent promptly; retain claim + closed delivery
    D -> D : late result revalidated against record/daemon/controller fences
    D -> H : resolve same launch/receipt then journaled E-stop if required
  end
  opt configured host requests stop of execution under permit
    SH -> D : host_stop (request/reference/auth encoding unpublished)
    D -> D : current permitted execution only; durably host-requested, distinct from owner cancel
    D -> H : E-stop / exec.stop; latest-receipt fence; account-wide scope
    H --> D : confirmed absence or unfinished/unknown evidence retaining claims
    note over D,SH : host_stop confers no start authority; pending E-stop continues identical arguments.
  end
  note over D,SR
    Dispatcher alone invokes the root launcher; host has no privileged start role.
    Lifecycle authorisation/budget, session permit, host_stop authentication,
    fence withdrawal, crash/receipt ordering and handoffs
    need joint publication and qualification; backend remains gated (§§12, 16).
    Controller-only re-adoption keeps execution_id and needs no permit action.
    Replacement uses new execution_id only under consent, prior absence and fresh checks.
    Retired one-shot orchestrator owner -> no restart; same session/op never duplicates successor.
    User-manager §7 R-FATE table defines survival/maintenance affected sets; no implicit adoption.
    Fresh runner checks exclusive native-session lock; native resume retains §12 rules.
    Log handoff remains unpublished (§16, question 5).
  end note
else default supervisor backend
  D -> B : fresh revocation.check exact chains, context start
  alt not_revoked and other start authority valid
    D -> D : service-UID supervisor -> root launcher -> agent-UID curator-run
    note over D,L : §5.3 one-shot intake / Decision 0021 / R-FD3 qualification gate remains required.
  else revoked / unavailable or other authority invalid
    D --> C : refuse before launch
  end
end
opt explicit stop / operator maintenance / exit / incident hard stop / recovery; runtime only for ordinary executions
  D -> H : exec.stop (journaled E-stop; current own generation/execution)\nTERM/grace/KILL UID + per-user domain; quiet-period absence; no state lock held
  alt termination observation unknown / contradictory or stop refused
    D -> D : retain state and capacity; same-effect recovery; never relaunch
  else termination confirmed
    H --> D : quiet-period account-wide absence confirmed
    D -> D : record outcome; applicable cleanup; terminal after confirmation
  end
end
D --> C : current execution record; events only behind later capability
note over D
  R-LOCK wait graph: state lock -> local journal/records; unlocked host -> dispatcher,
  unlocked dispatcher -> helper/launcher/broker. Bounded per-record markers/I/O; old writers fenced.
  Unfinished admitted stop is pending under receiver R-OUTCOME, not terminal refusal.
  R-GEN: external restore fence + independent coverage/reverse inventory; orphan decisions signed.
  R-REBIND: authorised renewal on same allocation, old tombstone; no wider scope/account recreation.
  R-TIME: watermark max expiry / min not_before; trusted advances only,
  expiry deletion also needs boot-inclusive elapsed lifetime; explicit stop stays reachable.
  Host reboot requester remains open; owner lifecycle consent bounds either candidate.
  Workplace backend is separate/gated: service-owned swarma-rb-exec, enforced helper v1.
  R-UNTRUSTED: workplace untrusted unless operator-admitted to trusted circle; slice 0/helper v0 refuse; no subscription binding/lease.
  Trusted-circle admission enables donor-side opt-ins only; workplace host boundaries stay.
  R-NET-TOOL/R-RANGE-DENY: workplace zero egress/no proxy; static range rule from v0.
  Web default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only; host boundaries stay.
  No direct/external-http-proxy binding for any platform-host account.
  N15 (2026-10-13): one listener per account_generation, bound to profile_ref; own port only.
  served_policy_digest and service_generation evidence; contract owned by N15.
  R-EXEC/R-VERIFY: OS exec allowlist + machine-selected immutable body pin.
  Full invocation/interpreted inputs qualified; worker-code execution/builds/tests off-host.
  R-CEILINGS: class minimums met by published host matrix; no OS-name ban.
  R-STANDING: host-local loop trusted only; digest-check surfaces on launch/restart/resume.
  R-TRANSFER: export obligation before retirement; workspace-transfer.puml.
  R-WATCH v0/S0a: affected-account journaled stop, admission hold, observer status only.
  No per-account egress-freeze or phone-alert promise; v1/S2 lifecycle open (§§7.3, 16).
  R-ALLSTOP: direct independent cuts/stops; receiver launch/create/ingress fence before absence.
  Fresh never-launched absence needs complete launch coverage.
  Every part including dispatcher reconciliation required before explicit recovery.
  Internal sweep never expires standing allocations or stops them for runtime.
  R-OPERATOR: swarma-operator never hosts harness sessions; operator authority stays there.
  Signed operator records: operator device key on phone + biometric/content confirmation, or terminal password/content confirmation.
  Every operator act/record from agent sessions refuses; command/signature formats unpublished (§§3.2, 16).
  swarma-observer reads dispatcher state without confirmation; no mutation authority.
  Standing retirement/re-creation is operator-only with signed record (§5.4).
  Maintenance: bounded authorized stop attempt; confirmed absence/reconciliation
  before mode/schema/binary change; retain standing allocations/identities; no live adoption.
  Restart needs fresh authority. Unknown/refused stop defers change (§11).
  Board/host clients never embed broker clients (§5.3).
  Exact later event payloads and recovery delivery remain unpublished (§§8, 12, 14).
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#83-socket-dispatch1 §8.3 socket]]
  [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#12-session-host-backend-later-activation-gate §12 backend]] / §§3.4, 7, 9, 11, 14
endlegend
@enduml
